 VALUES
('ab1fdcc4-b7e1-400e-a941-930d21f9fbf5'::uuid,'CPU scheduling','The operating system routine that selects which ready process receives CPU time and when.','Deciding which process receives the processor so competing programs can make progress.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.2, p.376; Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.1, p.35 (process scheduling routines); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.2, p.376; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('ddda418f-93f9-4cb6-ae67-a2e82500f678'::uuid,'System throughput','The number of processes or jobs a computer system completes in a given period of time.','The rate at which a computer completes processing work.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.2, p.377 (scheduling objective); Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.1, p.35 (scheduling routines); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.2, p.377; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('76e21603-60e6-479e-af69-f2bec0cff385'::uuid,'External fragmentation','A memory-management problem in which free memory is split into non-contiguous blocks, so a large contiguous block cannot be allocated.','Free space split across separated locations, which may impede allocating a large segment.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.4, p.385 (segmentation); Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.1, p.35 (memory management, paging and segmentation); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.4, p.385; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('431178b4-2df6-4a46-8cb2-7158fb1f2788'::uuid,'Hardware abstraction','The operating system hides hardware-specific details and provides a simpler interface for users and applications.','The OS presenting simple controls while performing more complicated device operations.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.376; Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.1, p.35 (user interface hides hardware complexity); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.376; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('22f64c0a-b444-45a0-87bd-8790a96b6afc'::uuid,'Kernel interrupt handling','The kernel receives an interrupt, identifies the appropriate interrupt handler and coordinates the response before normal processing continues.','Kernel processing of interrupt events requiring immediate attention.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.375; Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.1, p.35 (kernel interrupt handling and low-level scheduling); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.375; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('8f98dced-b223-487e-b287-1be8557efd2f'::uuid,'Cross-platform application compatibility','A virtual machine can run software designed for a different operating system by providing the required guest environment.','Executing software designed for another operating system in a compatible guest environment.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.2.2, p.393 (virtual-machine benefit); Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §15.1, p.34 (benefits of virtual machines); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.2.2, p.393; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('9c197a85-dad7-4400-a31b-4e6e7837123a'::uuid,'VM performance overhead','The reduction in speed that can occur because a virtual machine must run a guest operating system and manage virtual hardware on top of the host system.','Loss of performance compared with running the same software directly on compatible physical hardware.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.2.2, p.394 (virtual-machine limitation); Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §15.1, p.34 (limitations of virtual machines); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.2.2, p.394; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('36cb3e06-a2d6-48e1-b201-4e3502b6ec57'::uuid,'Operator precedence','The rules that determine the order in which operators are evaluated in an expression.','Rules specifying which arithmetic operation must be carried out before another.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.3.4, p.401; related to expression evaluation in Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.2, p.36; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.3.4, p.401; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('959da24d-450b-48c3-91d8-a3c2c507ace7'::uuid,'Input/output (I/O) management','An operating-system function that controls communication and data transfers between programs, memory and peripheral devices.','Coordinating data transfers involving peripherals such as keyboards, printers and storage drives.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.374 (operating-system function); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.374; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-'),
('2380f6b8-681b-477e-9993-83106d71e645'::uuid,'Command-line interface (CLI)','A user interface in which a user types text commands to control the operating system or an application.','A user interface issuing commands as typed text, contrasted with drag-and-drop interaction.','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.376 (user-interface type); related to Cambridge 9618 Syllabus 2027–2029, §16.1, p.35 (user interface); PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-','Hodder 9618 (Watson & Williams, 2019), §16.1.1, p.376; chapter detail; PDF:9618_Chapter_16.pdf; Drive:17qXAmcDsvLV96ytM5w75MWYNsGw9Buf-')
)
UPDATE public.glossary_terms AS g
SET definition_en=c.old_definition,
    source_ref=c.old_source,
    definition_evidence_status='supplementary_manual_review_required',
    is_glossary_visible=false
FROM changes AS c
WHERE g.id=c.id
  AND g.term=c.term
  AND g.definition_en=c.new_definition
  AND g.source_ref=c.new_source
  AND g.definition_evidence_status='supplementary_targeted_verified'
  AND g.is_glossary_visible=true
RETURNING g.id,g.term,g.definition_evidence_status,g.is_glossary_visible;
